(a) The scientific name of the fruit fly is **Drosophila melanogaster**.

(b) Thomas Hunt Morgan chose fruit flies because (any two):
- they can be **grown on a simple synthetic medium** in the laboratory;
- they **complete their life cycle in about two weeks**, so many generations can be studied quickly;
- a **single mating produces a large number of progeny** flies;
- there is a **clear differentiation of the sexes**: male and female flies are easily distinguishable;
- they show **many types of hereditary variations** that can be seen with low-power microscopes.
